body:
When a cell is in edit mode, clicking on the input field or the cell itself will trigger the `onRowClick` handler (if defined). This is likely unintended behavior - clicking within an editing cell should not trigger row click events. Consider adding logic to check if a cell is currently being edited (similar to how the code checks for buttons and checkboxes on lines 570-571) or adding `e.stopPropagation()` to the input's onClick handler.
```suggestion
                                onKeyDown={handleEditKeyDown}
                                onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}
```

The edit input is missing an `onBlur` handler to exit edit mode when the user clicks or tabs away from the cell. Currently, users can only save (Enter) or cancel (Escape) the edit. Without an onBlur handler, clicking outside the input cell leaves it in edit mode, which is inconsistent with standard spreadsheet behavior. Consider adding an onBlur handler that either auto-saves or cancels the edit based on the desired UX (the PR description mentions "No auto-save on blur" but there's no blur handler at all currently).
```suggestion
                                onKeyDown={handleEditKeyDown}
                                onBlur={() => {
                                  // Exit edit mode on blur without auto-saving
                                  setEditingCell(null);
                                  setEditValue('');
                                }}
```
